WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Sikhs believe that Guru Nanak had
an experience of God in a river.

2
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.920
Afterwards, they believe, he
spoke a short statement about God.

3
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.390
Today it is the very first
passage of the Sikh scripture,

4
00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.950
the Guru Granth Sahib.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.640
And many Sikhs recite it every morning.

6
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.060
How much can you say
about God in so few words,

7
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.240
and why say them every day?

8
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.370
In this mission, you'll
unpack the Mool Mantar,

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.210
one word at a time.

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.510
Then you'll see why Sikhs call
it the root of their faith,

11
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.730
and how it shapes the way they live.

12
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.600
Your mission: find out what
these few words say about God,

13
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.530
and why they matter so much.
